on\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0f952559140f1d03fdb954b4f0f865d7235837d01b340197898521c7eaf854c2","event_uuid":"f3228742-d0c5-4706-9a8b-46671ad5f01e","position":{"commit_sha":"42d73fa0c66108bbe856deb93e8a93602dbd1f0b","position":"1787470616605714001-f3228742-d0c5-4706-9a8b-46671ad5f01e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6ced7ca2ea16d479b3c837d436897e2356a9675d789fc14d1e1f81e82b5c5be5","event_uuid":"a4c36729-f9f6-4ced-be15-9fd8be307ee5","position":{"commit_sha":"2f91eb63f5346cd4710a7ae9f1d61c8d98213bb1","position":"1787470980378614001-a4c36729-f9f6-4ced-be15-9fd8be307ee5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"FORCE_CLAIM: plan-review gate bypassed by user approval — no plan-review attestation was verified. Reason: \"plan-review PASSED (verdict PASS, 0 blocking; verified_at_sha dc2f8098962) but attestation signing starved: 'generation remained unstable after 3 attempts' across review-plan + 3 sign-review retries under continuous multi-agent tracker write load. Same systemic starvation as 3235-8aaf and 9dc3-7d6c this session. Proceeding per operator remediation protocol (retry 2-3x then continue).\".","timestamp":1787460566902924001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"AUDIT (AC4) — binding_recovery.py:342-346 pending-recovery loop vs the per-JQL search memo:\n\nFINDING: unaffected by the memo; no change needed.\n\nProof:\n1. WITHIN a pass, the loop issues each JQL once per pending id: the primary 'labels = \"rebar-id:<local_id>\"' and the hyphen fallback are DISTINCT JQL strings, so neither can replay the other's cached answer, and neither is re-asked in the same pass.\n2. ACROSS passes, search_miss_count corroboration accumulates toward _MISSES_BEFORE_UNBIND — but each pass constructs a fresh client (and thus a fresh memo): reconcile_helpers.bind_operation_runtime (reconcile_helpers.py:675) composes 'the ONE operation runtime for this pass' per pass; _backend_registry.select_backend (_backend_registry.py:60-76) constructs a fresh backend on every call with no caching; the production entrypoint runs one reconcile_once per process (__main__.py:450). So repeated misses are genuinely fresh queries — the unbind threshold can never be satisfied by replays of one cached negative.\n\nThis lifetime proof is also recorded at the cache definition in acli.py (AcliClient.__init__, change 2146).","timestamp":1787461569277696001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"EVIDENCE OF COMPLETION — merged.\n\nChange: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2146 (LLM-Review+1, Verified+1, submitted; merged as 051e920b3b on main).\n\nWhat landed: AcliClient.invalidate_search_cache(jql=None) — the supported freshness door (per-JQL evict; full clear on None; never-searched evict is a no-op). _search_cache initialization moved into __init__ (search_issues drops its lazy hasattr branch — complexity ratchet reported the function as an allowed improvement). Client lifetime (one reconcile pass per instance, citing bind_operation_runtime and select_backend) documented at the cache definition; negative-caching hazard documented in the search_issues docstring. Both reach-in sites migrated onto the door via callable-guarded lookup: access_check.py JQL retry loop and _fresh_search in tests/integration/test_reconcile_live_e2e.py.\n\nACs:\n- AC1 (lifetime answered + documented at cache definition): DONE — __init__ comment cites bind_operation_runtime (reconcile_helpers.py:675) and select_backend (_backend_registry.py:60-76).\n- AC2 (door exists; no reach-in outside acli.py): DONE — grep -rn _search_cache src tests shows only acli.py + docstring mentions; pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_acli_search_cache_freshness.py: 4 passed (memoized negative, evict makes negative-to-positive flip visible, full clear, no-op edge — all counted at the _run seam).\n- AC3 (negative-caching documented): DONE — search_issues docstring names the hazard and the door (bug d30c).\n- AC4 (binding_recovery audit): DONE — proof recorded in the prior AUDIT comment on this ticket.\n\nGates: targeted 81 passed (freshness + sweep + timeout + access-check seam + preflight); make lint (complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0); make typecheck clean; CI Verified+1. Rate-limit sweep classifies invalidate_search_cache NON-MUTATING (pure memo evict).","timestamp":1787470591011679001}],"created_at":1787172515610120001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1c5f19d6-d37e-4241-93b9-9079688cfc50","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"d30c-f491-395f-432e"},{"link_uuid":"6418ff58-0559-4a92-a9ab-a8b9b6673268","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b1a4-2c5a-3cba-4309"},{"link_uuid":"00952762-8e23-4c65-a2ff-0d5277caa293","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e7fb-17a3-4879-4ded"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`AcliClient.search_issues` (`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py:398-453`)\nmemoizes its full result set per JQL string in `self._search_cache` — an unbounded dict with\nno TTL and no invalidation anywhere in the class — and it caches negative (empty) answers too.\nThe docstring scopes the cache to \"avoid redundant fetches when the caller paginates\", but\nnothing enforces that scope: any caller that re-asks the same JQL over time on one client gets\na permanently stale answer. Proven root cause of bug d30c (dutiable-shaded-honeyeater), where\nan index-visibility poll re-issued two constant JQLs on one client and only the first attempt\never reached Jira. The only correct handling in the tree reaches into the private attribute\nfrom outside the class: `access_check.py:176-178` does `cache.pop(jql, None)` before each\nretry, and the d30c fix (`tests/integration/test_reconcile_live_e2e.py` `_fresh_search`,\n~:393-416) copies that reach-in. The freshness invariant is undocumented, unenforced, and\nsatisfied only by encapsulation violations.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. **Establish client lifetime and document it at the cache definition.** Evidence already\n   read from the tree: `reconcile_helpers.bind_operation_runtime`\n   (`reconcile_helpers.py:675`) composes \"the ONE operation runtime for this pass\" per pass;\n   `_backend_registry.select_backend` (`_backend_registry.py:60-76`) constructs a fresh\n   backend on every call (no caching); the production entrypoint runs one\n   `reconcile.reconcile_once` per process invocation (`rebar_reconciler/__main__.py:450`).\n   So an `AcliClient` — and its `_search_cache` — lives at most ONE reconcile pass. Record\n   this at the cache definition in `acli.py` and in the audit comment on this ticket.\n2. **Add the supported freshness door**: an `AcliClient.invalidate_search_cache(jql: str |\n   None = None)` method — evicts the one JQL entry when given, clears the whole memo when\n   `None`. Chosen over a `fresh=True` kwarg because it is purely additive (no\n   `search_issues` signature change on the transport port, `_backend.py`) and matches the\n   evict-then-search shape both existing call sites already use. Move `self._search_cache`\n   initialization into `AcliClient.__init__` so the method needs no `hasattr` dance (and\n   `search_issues` drops its lazy-init branch — a complexity improvement).\n3. **Migrate both reach-in sites onto the door**: `access_check.py:176-178` and\n   `_fresh_search` in `tests/integration/test_reconcile_live_e2e.py` call\n   `invalidate_search_cache(jql)` via a callable-guarded lookup (both sites accept arbitrary\n   client classes/stubs today, so the guarded lookup preserves that tolerance while using\n   the supported name).\n4. **Document the negative-caching hazard** in the `search_issues` docstring: negative\n   (empty) results are cached; a caller that re-asks the same JQL for freshness must call\n   `invalidate_search_cache` first.\n5. **Audit `binding_recovery.py:342-346`**: the pending-recovery loop issues each\n   `labels = \"rebar-id:<local_id>\"` JQL once per pending id per pass (the hyphen fallback is\n   a distinct JQL string), and its `search_miss_count` corroboration accumulates ACROSS\n   passes — where each pass constructs a fresh client (step 1), so repeated misses are\n   genuinely fresh queries and `_MISSES_BEFORE_UNBIND` cannot be satisfied by replays of one\n   cached answer. Record this proof in the ticket comment and in the cache-definition note.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py` — init cache in `__init__`, add\n  `invalidate_search_cache`, document lifetime + negative caching in the docstrings.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/access_check.py` — migrate the JQL retry loop's\n  reach-in onto `invalidate_search_cache`.\n- `tests/integration/test_reconcile_live_e2e.py` — migrate `_fresh_search` onto\n  `invalidate_search_cache`.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_acli_search_cache_freshness.py` — new unit tests for the\n  memo + door.\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit tests (new file, subprocess stubbed at the `AcliClient._run` seam, counting invocations):\n\n- Happy: two `search_issues` calls with the same JQL run ONE subprocess (pins the existing\n  memo, including a negative first answer staying cached).\n- Freshness door: `invalidate_search_cache(jql)` then re-search re-runs the subprocess and\n  returns the refreshed answer (a negative-to-positive flip becomes visible — the d30c\n  class).\n- Full clear: `invalidate_search_cache()` empties the memo for all JQLs.\n- Edge: invalidating a never-searched JQL is a no-op (no raise, memo unchanged).\n\nExisting coverage guards the migrations: the access-check retry loop and live-E2E poll tests\nkeep passing with the reach-in replaced.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The `AcliClient` lifetime question is answered (one pass per instance in production)\n      and documented at the cache definition in `acli.py` — checked by reading the committed\n      docstring/comment citing `bind_operation_runtime` and `select_backend`.\n- [x] `invalidate_search_cache(jql=None)` exists and `access_check.py` plus the d30c E2E\n      poll use it instead of popping `_search_cache` directly — checked by\n      `grep -rn \"_search_cache\" src tests` showing no reach-in outside `acli.py`, and by\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_acli_search_cache_freshness.py`.\n- [x] The `search_issues` docstring states that negative results are cached and repeat-query\n      callers must invalidate first — checked by reading the docstring.\n- [x] `binding_recovery.py:342-346` is audited: the proof that per-pass client construction\n      makes cross-pass miss corroboration fresh is recorded as a comment on this ticket —\n      checked by the comment's presence.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py","reason":"init cache in __init__, add invalidate_search_cache, document lifetime and negative caching"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/access_check.py","reason":"migrate JQL retry loop reach-in onto invalidate_search_cache"},{"path":"tests/integration/test_reconcile_live_e2e.py","reason":"migrate _fresh_search onto invalidate_search_cache"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_acli_search_cache_freshness.py","reason":"new unit tests for the memo and freshness door"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","b1a4-2c5a-3cba-4309"],["relates_to","e7fb-17a3-4879-4ded"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"fc17712d-5fb5-4143-9c07-b428bc8dec62","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3288-aa58-54d0-4c19","ticket_type":"task","title":"Give AcliClient's per-JQL search memo a supported freshness door (it caches negatives forever)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["abaa838d-cee3-45d8-970b-5c2b4eb2b68e","d7cff753-7787-4bdf-b073-abc2586cc44d","d5bed9f6-752f-4ae6-9dce-90a042b302ee","fc17712d-5fb5-4143-9c07-b428bc8dec62","a4c6da03-1672-4fbb-a941-2e5943a7febe","6f3acbde-8744-42f5-9d60-7641731d128c","6418ff58-0559-4a92-a9ab-a8b9b6673268","00952762-8e23-4c65-a2ff-0d5277caa293","f71771bf-550a-44be-b023-839ee02732c8","f3228742-d0c5-4706-9a8b-46671ad5f01e","a4c36729-f9f6-4ced-be15-9fd8be307ee5"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787470980378614002,"uuid":"1039c897-a026-4974-b99c-efd68435643a"}